;; spec:   stdlib §2.3 (Collection s r e: a Map's e is a Pair), §5.5 S4 (a vector entry waits for L23)
;; expect: reject
;; error:  cannot unify i64 with (Pair i64 i64)
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: into
;; (into to c) needs c's elements to be the elements the target's conj takes:
;; for a Map that is a Pair. Clojure also takes a two-element vector, (into {}
;; [[1 2]]), which two instances of one head would need (L23, the open case
;; 903); a source of plain integers is a type error under both.
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq fib.coll))

(defun main () -> i64
  (count (into (empty {1 2}) [1 2])))
